From 78a23c8b3a79e147b8c1ceee152759b8ea6913da Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 20:47:22 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] feat(tools): a tool carries cutting data per workpiece
 material

A tool gains a per-material table of spindle rpm and feed, keyed by the
built-in work-material groups. The tool's own rpm/feed stay the running
numbers the post reads and the fallback. A row moves them only through
a command, one undo step each: SetWorkMaterial re-seeds the tools with a
row and their ops' milling feed, AddTool starts on the document
material's row, a table edit in ChangeTool loads it, a tool retarget
and the quick-adds seed the op feed. Nothing moves on load.

The file key cutting_data is additive and written only when stated, so
a tool without rows saves byte for byte as before (no version step).
An unknown material word or a bad row is refused by name. The tool
editor edits the rows under a collapsed header; MCP add_tool's
definition takes the list.

Fixes #890

